    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d322">

                <pb facs="0547" n="501" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg501"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5914/30½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State ad interim
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-06-16">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">16 June, 1915</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have read these papers
                    through with close attention, and thank you for handing them to me.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d322-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>As I said to you yesterday, I am, and have long been, deeply interested in the
                    purchase of the Danish West Indies. I hope that you will take the matter up very
                    seriously and that it may be possible to have a concrete proposal, if possible
                    in the form of a treaty, to lay before the Senate at its next session.</p>
                <p>Cordially and Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d322-f1" n="1" xml:id="d322-f1-content">
